It looks like you successfully saved your rules! The cat command shows you have explicitly added rules for two major Android vendors:

* 0e8d: MediaTek devices
* 18d1: Google / Nexus / Pixel devices (and many generic Android bootloaders)

Because you used MODE="0666", any user on your laptop has read and write permissions for these devices, which is great for debugging.
Now, you just need to make your laptop apply these new rules so it recognizes your phone. Run these two commands in your terminal:

sudo udevadm control --reload-rules
sudo udevadm trigger

Once you've done that, plug in your Android phone via USB, make sure USB Debugging is turned on in your phone's settings, and test the connection.
